"title": "Find K Pairs with Smallest Sums",
"diff": "Medium",
"topic": "heaps",
"pattern": "K-way merge",
"hook": "From two sorted arrays, return the k pairs (one number from each) with the smallest sums.",
"brute": "Generate all m × n pairs and sort: O(mn log mn).",
"insight": "Think of rows: row i is <code>nums1[i]</code> paired with <code>nums2[0], nums2[1], …</code>, already sorted by sum. Merging sorted rows with a heap (like merging k sorted lists): start with the first pair of each row, pop the smallest, then push the next pair from the same row.",
"steps": [
"Heap of <code>(nums1[i] + nums2[0], i, 0)</code> for the first k rows.",
"Pop the smallest; record the pair.",
"Push <code>(i, j + 1)</code> if it exists.",
"Stop after k pairs."
],
"code": "class Solution:\n    def kSmallestPairs(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int], k: int) -> List[List[int]]:\n        heap = [(nums1[i] + nums2[0], i, 0) for i in range(min(k, len(nums1)))]\n        heapq.heapify(heap)\n        res = []\n        while heap and len(res) < k:\n            _, i, j = heapq.heappop(heap)\n            res.append([nums1[i], nums2[j]])\n            if j + 1 < len(nums2):            # next pair in the same \"row\"\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (nums1[i] + nums2[j + 1], i, j + 1))\n        return res",
"time": "O(k log k)",
"space": "O(k)",
"run": "Solution().kSmallestPairs([1, 7, 11], [2, 4, 6], 3)",
"expect": "[[1, 2], [1, 4], [1, 6]]",
"plans": [
"top150"
],
